Subject: [PATCH 2/2] infra/hosts/beastie: Document installing the mail ports
To: lab@lists.p7x.dev
Cc: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Change-Id: ukuzptmwxvppvnszwyxxrqprlynvyokm
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 04:27:05 +0000

The mail ports reach beastie only through a boot environment built
from its ports list, so a running beastie lacks them until the next
one. Nothing said so, or how to get them sooner, and the mail checks
then fail on a host that cannot run them.
---
change-id: ukuzptmwxvppvnszwyxxrqprlynvyokm

 infra/hosts/beastie/README.org | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/infra/hosts/beastie/README.org b/infra/hosts/beastie/README.org
index d2bd8e4e..942d9539 100644
--- a/infra/hosts/beastie/README.org
+++ b/infra/hosts/beastie/README.org
@@ -9,7 +9,12 @@ spec is =../../../jails/instances/lab-mail/spec.org=. It is set up in
 three layers, from most shared to most specific:
 
 1. Ports. mail/isync, mail/msmtp, and mail/notmuch are in =ports=,
-   like any other package beastie needs.
+   like any other package beastie needs, so a boot environment built
+   from =ports= has them. Until beastie runs one built since they
+   were added, install them on the running system:
+   #+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
+   doas pkg install isync msmtp notmuch
+   #+END_EXAMPLE
 2. The notmuch package. =dotfiles/notmuch= installs the lab-mail
    profile's hooks, which every host that reads the list shares, and
    samples of each config:
